Docker testing : 

Build the Docker Image:
-----------------------

>> docker build -t ecommerce-ui:v1 .

Run the Docker image:
-----------------------

>> docker run -d \
     --name ecommerce-ui-test
     -p 4000:4000 
     ecommerce-ui:v1

Check the containes and their logs
----------------------------------
>> docker ps
>> docker logs ecommerce-ui-test

Test the application
---------------------------------

Test the liveness endpoint
--------------------------
>> curl -i http://localhost:4000/health/live
Expected HTTP status 200 OK

Expected JSON response:

{
  "status": "alive",
  "service": "ecommerce-ui"
}


This confirms that the gateway is responding to HTTP requests
it does not verify that all the backend microservice are available

Test 2: Test the frontend
--------------------------
>> curl -I http://localhost:4000/

Expected HTTP status:
200 OK

This confirms that the application responds to a request for the homepage.
It does not guarantee that every frontend feature works.


